WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.795
Dear Netflix and Amazon

00:00:02.795 --> 00:00:05.785
I am just a simple, passionate anime fan

00:00:05.785 --> 00:00:08.895
But today I bring the sentiment of many of our community at large

00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:11.935
and we have a bone to pick with the services you provide

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.860
when streaming anime online.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.600
I am not the first to talk about this or make the point I am about to make

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.940
and I doubt i will be the last either

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.620
But I wanted to lay down a short and concise message as I could

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:25.760
for the each of you

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:31.520
with constructive criticisms that I and many of us in the anime community share towards your services

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.400
how you can improve them and why you should care.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.480
Because i don't think the problem comes from bad business practices

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:43.415
but more stems from the both of you stepping into a new market which you may not fully understand yet.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.900
And bringing the models you have used previously, thinking that it will be just as effective here

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.820
which is why i wanted to address you directly.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:52.400
Let's start with you Netflix

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.720
which if by luck anyone for Amazon is watching this, feel free to skip to the time stamp shown on the screen for that segment

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:04.060
Now Netflix, the problem we have of your service is very simple and easy to fix

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:07.040
So let me lay this out in a single sentence

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.960
Please simulcast the anime that you license

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.195
I have a huge respect for what you've done

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.040
and how you revolutionize the online streaming platform

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.700
and how we consume media in this modern day

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.100
and you of the seats taking big strides to help grow

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.080
and become an actual part of the anime industry

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.400
releasing your Netflix original shows by each season

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.200
at once was incredibly forethinking

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.780
that ties with modern binge-watching culture

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:37.280
but this model simply DOES NOT work for currently airing anime

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.420
that you license

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.920
And there are two main reasons for this

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:42.700
No.1 Piracy

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:49.260
At the moment, the only competitor you have against the anime you license is the pirate streaming sites and torrents

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.000
and they will always win

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.900
because they are the only service available when these shows are airing

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.900
I trust that you of all companies will understand

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.380
people won't be deterred from piracy just because there is no legal options available

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.505
If fans really want to watch a show

00:02:04.505 --> 00:02:07.235
even hardcore ones will turn to piracy

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.255
because you are holding onto anime for months after they air

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.960
and this is true for every community

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.015
Imagine if you will that you have the rights to a show like Game of Thrones

00:02:16.015 --> 00:02:18.995
and while little is airing you held onto it until this season ended

00:02:18.995 --> 00:02:21.715
Can you imagine how many more millions

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.160
of people would turn to piracy to see the show

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.435
Just because they know itself but not available to  any legal means

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:30.980
you release some of your American shows weekly to combat this problem anyway

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.535
and the same theory should apply to the anime community

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:36.600
Simulcasting doesn't seem to be a initiative for your Japanese division

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.025
which is putting the episodes up as they air

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:41.460
So why is it not the case internationally?

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.155
I am sure you have the resources needed to be able to subtitle them on time

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.560
And if you doubt, it is something that'd be a low investment for a high return.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:53.500
No.2 It kills the possible reach of the show that you license in our community

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:56.575
This may be a bit harder to comprehend at first

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.380
but the anime community works a bit differently than other audiences you are used to

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.235
In terms of our entertainment

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.720
we move on a lot faster

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.695
just because of the sheer number of new shows available to us every season

00:03:06.695 --> 00:03:09.385
We can get up to 40 new shows

00:03:09.385 --> 00:03:10.780
every THREE months

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.600
Now only a few of those shows will actually get popular

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.120
But because of the seasonal cycle

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:17.920
the shelf-life of a show is very low

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.380
Any show, no matter how popular it is,

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.420
Attack on Titan

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:22.580
One Punch Man

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:25.300
loses momentum very quickly after they stop airing

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.800
because the community are focusing on the new shows in the new season

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.920
And just because you hold on to a show

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:32.860
doesn't mean people will wait for it

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:36.680
A lot of people will just more likely watch something else that season

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:39.600
Shows get popular fast because we love to discuss them

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:45.040
And way more than other mediums popularity spread through word of mouth of the fans and the communities

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:50.000
and this makes sense because no mainstream outlet regularly covers anime shows

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:50.720
And if they do

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.900
it's because we have made enough of a noise about it

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:55.100
as we are still a niche community

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.180
These are our water cooler discussion

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.760
and what you've done by keeping your shows is allow other shows to be discussed around that water cooler

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:02.760
and because of this

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:08.680
the anime that you license WILL never and HAVE never had the same reach that they could have had

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.440
Little Witch Academia had bundles of hype when it was announced

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:17.700
which has never probably been met even after you released the first half now a good two season after it started airing

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:23.100
and releasing Kakegurui in 2018 is gonna do absolutely nothing but hurt it for you end

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.860
Considering it's actually one of the most watched anime of this season

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:30.180
I understand the model of releasing all episodes at once keeps single watch time in your site higher

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.740
which is your overall strategy

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.060
And it is working well

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:38.580
I cannot stress enough how much respect I have for the bundles of original anime you are funding yourselves that you've just announced

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.580
and I am so glad that you have made this initiative

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:45.220
which is why this only applies to the shows that you license that air on Japanese TV

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.680
Not one you produce and fund yourselves

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:52.100
such as Blame! and the upcoming Devilman that you completely own the exclusive rights for

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:56.540
But you can easily increase traffic and views for these shows that you license every season

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.840
by simply releasing them while they air

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.220
I know you probably have a larger mainstream audience in mind and not just anime fans

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:06.860
But if you are going to get into the market of licensing new currently airing anime

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.040
the demographic will appreciate it,

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:13.540
understand it and create significant buzz on the off chance that you do license a super hit

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.500
is US

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.020
As we did with Attack on Titan

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.020
As we did with One Punch Man

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.720
and by denying this you are not only denying this community

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:24.940
but you are also denying yourselves from traffic and a higher chance of having a hit show

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.380
So once again

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.420
Please Simulcast the anime

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:30.760
That You License

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.560
And now to you, Amazon

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.420
which if there were someone from Netflix watching

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:36.420
you could skip ahead to the time stamp for my closing statement

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.800
Amazon you recently launch animeStrike

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.600
a separately branded service simply for anime

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:45.560
and you are actually simulcasting shows you have which I appreciate

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:49.360
The main criticism with your service, however, is a bit more complicated to fix

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.720
as it is mainly based on your pricing structure

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:53.720
but it essentially  boils down to this:

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:57.160
Please Provide A Single Separate

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.660
Pricing Plan For animeStrike

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:03.920
At the moment to get access to your service your customers need to have an Amazon prime account

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.160
which is $10 a month

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.500
and then pay an extra $5 on top of that to get animeStrike

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:12.100
Totalling at $15 a month or $160 a year

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.480
Compared to the $60 a year your major competitors offer

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:20.320
That is $15 a month to essentially simulcast your exclusive seasonal titles

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:24.540
because you know most of the value in that price goes into your exclusives

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.240
as your overall selection at the moment,

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.200
to put it bluntly, is far more limited than what your competitors offer

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.240
at a lower rate

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:32.620
and this right is

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:36.900
the mentality you are fighting against when the vast majority of anime fans view your service

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:40.700
because really thinking about this all the benefits you get for that $15

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.660
with all the other services you provide

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:45.880
overall is completely worth the price in my opinion

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:48.740
The problem lies with your pricing structure and buyer psychology

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:53.200
because to us we don't see all the other benefits in that $15

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.040
many people are only interested in anime

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:58.520
and $15 is extremely high entry barrier

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.475
from the perspective of us anime fans

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.860
it feels like we are just an afterthought

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.940
a quick cash-grab on top of all the other services you provide

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.060
and because of this there is an air of negative stigma within the community

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.340
when we see your service

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:14.420
At the moment your model only targets people who have an existing prime account

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.940
which makes sense that you want to market your other services

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:17.440
HOWEVE

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:21.860
rather than incentivising people to get a prime account for these exclusive titles

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.060
you are alienating anyone who doesn't

00:07:24.065 --> 00:07:26.995
because unlike your HBO service for example

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.080
which has HBO go as an alternative

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:32.560
for your exclusive anime there is no alternative for audiences to go to

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.480
and because of that this entry barrier smells of greed

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:41.200
by simply offering the choice of having a single pricing plan just for animeStrike

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:43.420
you can hit every demographic

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.660
you are already marketing to a niche

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.580
and by making this niche even smaller

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.820
you are preventing your own market from growing

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:52.740
You know how valuable these exclusive titles are

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:55.800
but by alienating the market who sees the value in them

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.240
Who really wins?

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:58.160
THE PIRATES

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:00.420
You can even price the animeStrike-only plan more

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:03.020
if you don't wanna set at the base rate of $5

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.120
you can maybe even take it as higher as $7 a month

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.440
Then make it so if you have an amazonPrime and an animeStrike package

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:11.240
it is the $15 you are offering now

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.700
That is far more appealing to everyone because the point is

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.060
the consumers have a choice

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:19.180
and you are incentivising people to use all your serivces

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.055
rather than alienating them

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.005
And I guarantee you will have a far larger share of the market

00:08:24.005 --> 00:08:26.140
by simply offering this choice

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:28.760
while also getting rid of that negative stigma

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.900
there have been other criticisms of your service

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:31.860
but right now

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:36.140
this is the BIGGEST and most PRESSING problem our community feels needs fixing

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:37.755
so I reiterate

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:40.660
Please Provide A Single Separate

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.720
Pricing Plan For animestrike

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:45.820
Now I understand that the moment that we are just a niche market

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:48.360
compared to all the other shows and services you provide

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:49.280
which is true

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:51.600
But anime is growing at a rapid rate

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:53.220
and you must realize it too

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.020
if you are willing to the money you have

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:56.340
to get a foot in this industry

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.200
so I ask

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.880
What is the point of investing your hard-earned money

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:03.260
into this market, this community, this fandom

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:08.260
if you aren't going to see the true return on the very demographic you are marketing these services towards

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.120
it is not tell to winningest in our end

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:13.780
I can assure you as I am certain some of your competitors in this sphere can attest to

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.815
But it is out of a lack of understanding of our community at large

00:09:16.815 --> 00:09:19.735
which I am hoping you now have a better idea of

00:09:19.735 --> 00:09:22.585
by not providing a service the community is satisfied with

00:09:22.585 --> 00:09:25.035
it is not so much you are taking revenue away from your competitors

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:28.260
it's more you are putting traffic to illegal sources

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:29.200
that hurt the industry

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:32.420
and you are also stunting the possible growth of these shows and fandom

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:35.040
and thus the market you can possible have

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:38.160
I say this as someone who does want everyone to do the best they can

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:40.880
and promote healthy competition between companies

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:44.000
as i fear at it is now the industry will take a step backward

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.600
rather than continuing to take that step forward

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:51.480
So that is why I hope this message finds the right person or people

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.840
because i am not sure what the right way to contact

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:55.800
either Amazon or Netflix are

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:59.340
both companies are so big I don't even know what the right point of contact is

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:00.300
for these suggestions

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:03.940
So all I can do is send this video to the appropriate feedback forums

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.820
and also send it to their corresponding Twitter accounts

00:10:05.825 --> 00:10:08.775
and I am sure many fans who share my sentiments

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:10.380
and have seen this video will do the same

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.500
in hopes that I could make a change

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.340
It is a long shot, I know

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:19.220
You are both multi billion dollar companies with your own models and strategies

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:21.840
but if our community don't even try to make a noise

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.760
there is absolutely no hope that we will ever get heard

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:29.115
So to any customer service workers or social media managers on the Twitter account

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:31.240
all I ask if you get this far

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.500
is that you do everything you can to get this to the right person or people

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.500
when you are discussing public feedback

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:39.560
So that even if the companies don't do everything we have suggested

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:40.520
at the very least

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.720
if we can get some kind of acknowledgement and feedback

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.720
so we know that our voices are heard

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:47.060
As I know from my own corporate experience

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:50.380
that change takes a long time in these big companies

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:51.560
It is a long shot

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:52.340
But hey

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:53.880
it is at least woth a try

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:57.940
Also just in case there is anyone who thinks I am doing this for a quick monetary gain

00:10:57.940 --> 00:11:01.660
I have removed all ads from this video and any potential sponsorships I could have had

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.860
as I just want to get the message across

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:05.400
to anyone else watching this

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.040
this isn't a call to boycott these services

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:11.120
nor is it want to promote piracy or harass any companies

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:14.140
but if you do want to get you opinion out ina constructive way

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:18.620
I will put all of additional information I can find about contacting them in the description below

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:20.040
Thank you for your time

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:21.380
Yours faithfully,

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:25.800
a frustrated but hopeful and passionate anime fan

